    "information_card_igAJVJ": {
      "type": "information-card",
      "blocks": {
        "card_9m7djb": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/1.png",
            "eyebrow": "",
            "title": "Protects at the Source",
            "text": "<p>Sperm health is a cellular problem. Developing sperm are vulnerable to oxidative damage for roughly 74–90 days before they ever show up on a lab report. Astaxanthin reaches inside the cell and shields them while they’re still forming.</p>"
          }
        },
        "card_dTUAaG": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/2_f3a0691d-e128-4bda-9344-a430b1cbe76a.png",
            "eyebrow": "",
            "title": "The Hidden Driver: Oxidative Stress",
            "text": "<p>Global sperm counts have fallen an estimated 50–62% since 1973, and the decline has accelerated since 2000. Oxidative stress is one of the most consistently cited mechanisms behind it. Astaxanthin is one of the most powerful inflammation and oxidative-stress suppressors ever measured, with 30+ years of research backing it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "card_hWhKrE": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/3.png",
            "eyebrow": "",
            "title": "Backed by Earth's Longest-Living People",
            "text": "<p>Astaxanthin is what gives salmon their pink color, flamingos their red, and the people of Okinawa, Japan their place as the longest-living humans on Earth. They get it daily through their seafood diet. They live longer than anyone.</p>"
          }
        },
        "card_DLtUhH": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/4.png",
            "eyebrow": "",
            "title": "Reaches What Nothing Else Can",
            "text": "<p>Zinc floats in your bloodstream. Folic acid gets processed and flushed. A major 2,300-couple clinical trial found the standard zinc-and-folic-acid combo did nothing for semen quality or live birth rates. Astaxanthin is fat-soluble and water-soluble — the only compound that physically crosses the cell membrane and works from the inside.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "card_9m7djb",
        "card_dTUAaG",
        "card_hWhKrE",
        "card_DLtUhH"
      ],
